<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's TGS says issued $50 mln bonds.</title>
<headline>Argentina's TGS says issued $50 mln bonds.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine gas transport company Transportadora de Gas del Sur (TGS) said Tuesday it issued $50 million in short-term bonds June 25 as part of a $150 million program.</p>
<p>TGS said it issued $30 million in series F bonds due September 23, 1997, at 98.58 percent, and $20 million in series G bonds due September 26, 1997, at 98.54 percent.  </p>
<p>The bonds were placed by BA Securities and Merrill Lynch Securities Inc, TGS said in a news release.</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
